Third-party agent marks

The logos in this folder belong to their owners. They are not covered by the
MIT licence of this repository. They are shown on the landing page, in one
strip and in one color, to say which coding agents Keep the Why can be
installed on. Nothing here claims endorsement by or affiliation with any of
these projects or companies.

Origin, fetched 2026-10-07:

- All files except pi.svg: the agent strip on https://www.skills.sh/
  (/agents/<name>.svg), the agents listed there at the time. skills.sh shows
  them under "Available for these agents"; the landing page makes the same
  use of them.
- pi.svg: Simple Icons (https://simpleicons.org/?q=pi), CC0, the mark of Pi
  (https://pi.dev/).

The files are stored as received, byte for byte. The page recolors them at
render time with a CSS mask, which keeps the shape and drops the tile; the
files themselves are not edited.

If you own one of these marks and want it removed or shown differently, open
an issue at https://github.com/oliver-zehentleitner/maity/issues and it will
be done file by file, no questions asked.
